**Game Design Document - Simple Image-Based Puzzle Game**  

**Game Title:** *Image Match-Up*  
**Description:**  
A simple memory-matching game where the player must find and match pairs of images. The game will use a set of predefined image files (e.g., `image.jpg`) and display them in a grid. The player clicks on two images to reveal them, and if they match, they remain visible. If not, they are hidden again. The game ends when all pairs are matched.  

**Core Features:**  
- A 4x4 grid of image cards  
- Image file handling (loading, saving, and referencing)  
- Matching logic  
- Timer and score tracking  
- Simple text-based UI (console or basic GUI)  

**Technical Stack:**  
- Python  
- Pygame (for basic GUI and image handling)  
- File I/O operations (reading and writing image files)  

**Directory Structure:**  
```
game/
│
├── images/
│   ├── image.jpg
│   └── ... (other images)
│
├── game.py
├── README.md
└── assets/
    └── ... (other assets)
``
